```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>

int countOccurrences(const std::string& text, const std::string& pattern) {
    int count = 0;
    size_t pos = 0;
    while ((pos = text.find(pattern, pos)) != std::string::npos) {
        ++count;
        pos += pattern.length(); // Move past the found pattern to avoid overlapping counts
    }
    return count;
}
```

This function `countOccurrences` efficiently counts how many times a `pattern` string appears within a larger `text` string. It uses `string::find` to locate the pattern, incrementing the `count` each time and updating the search position (`pos`) to avoid overlapping matches. It returns the total occurrence count.

