import java.util.Arrays;

public class Median {
    public static double findMedian(double[] arr) {
        Arrays.sort(arr);
        int n = arr.length;
        if (n % 2 == 0) {
            return (arr[n / 2 - 1] + arr[n / 2]) / 2.0;
        } else {
            return arr[n / 2];
        }
    }
}
```

This code first sorts the input array. If the array's length is even, it averages the two middle elements.  Otherwise (odd length), it returns the middle element directly.  Sorting ensures accurate median calculation.  The return type is `double` to handle potential decimal values.

